From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wshom: WScript.Shell's environments, special folders, shortcuts, RegDelete, LogEvent, AppActivate and SendKeys

WScript.Shell is the object most scripts start from, and much of it was
E_NOTIMPL: SendKeys and AppActivate (how scripts drive other programs),
RegDelete, LogEvent, Exec's ExitCode, an environment's Count, For Each,
Remove and assignment (every Environment() was the process's), the
special folders but three, their Count and For Each, and a shortcut's
Description, Hotkey, TargetPath, FullName, RelativePath and Load;
CreateShortcut on an existing shortcut did not read it.

- Environment("System" | "User" | "Volatile" | "Process"; none: the
  system's, as on Windows NT): the registry's (Session Manager\Environment,
  HKCU\Environment, HKCU\Volatile Environment) or the process's; values
  read back as stored; setting or removing one in the system's or user's
  tells running programs (WM_SETTINGCHANGE "Environment"); Count, length
  and For Each ("NAME=value").
- SpecialFolders: the sixteen of Windows Script Host, by name or position,
  an unknown name empty; Count, For Each.
- Shortcuts: CreateShortcut reads an existing one; Description, Hotkey
  ("ALT+CTRL+K", read and set), TargetPath, FullName, RelativePath, Load.
- RegDelete deletes a value, or a key ("...\"); root names are matched
  without case ("hkcu\..."). An unknown RegWrite type is E_INVALIDARG.
- LogEvent writes to the Application log from the "WSH" source.
- Exec(...).ExitCode is the program's exit code (0 while it runs).
- AppActivate: a window by its title (exact, then its start, then its
  end) or by process id, restored and brought forward.
- SendKeys: the Visual Basic SendKeys syntax -- +, ^, % and ~, {KEY} and
  {KEY n} names, {F1}..{F24}, {+}-style escapes, (groups) -- typed into
  the active window with SendInput; characters the layout lacks are sent
  as themselves.

Wine's wshom tests: no failures, as before.

Gate: test/wshshell-gate.sh (Xvfb, the shell's desktop, cscript with
test/wshshell.vbs and test/wshshell-target.c). Mutants
SG_MUTANT_PROCESS_ENV_ONLY, SG_MUTANT_NO_SENDKEYS (wshom.ocx/shell.c).
